# Experiment 2 (odds), re-run against ratchet v0.8.
#
# The v0 run of this experiment needed a project-local tools/ratchet-check.js
# -- 77 lines -- plus a tools/seed.js, to say four things. Every one of the
# four was the same shape: run a command, pull a number out of what it
# printed, assert the number sits in a band anchored to a published table.
# That shape is the vocabulary now, so the plumbing is gone and the four
# subjects are the sentences below.
#
# The bands are unchanged from the v0 run. They come from outside this
# repository -- published blackjack basic-strategy tables and the Monty Hall
# result -- which is the point: a check that merely re-encoded the fix would
# prove nothing.

heuristic basic-edge
  run      node blackjack.js basic.json 6 0.75 flat 300000
  seed     20260905
  timeout  600000
  applies  when blackjack.js exists
  measure  edge  number after "edge:"
  rule     edge is between -0.03 and 0.015
  because  every published basic-strategy table puts the house edge for these
  because  rules near -0.005; fifteen times that is a simulator bug, not variance

heuristic solver-grade
  run      node blackjack.js output.json 1 0.5 flat 300000
  seed     20260905
  timeout  600000
  applies  when output.json exists
  measure  edge  number after "edge:"
  rule     edge is between -0.03 and 0.01
  because  a solved table graded against its own solver should land near the
  because  published edge; a throw or a wild number means the grader broke

heuristic monty-hall
  run      node deal.js
  seed     20260905
  timeout  600000
  applies  when deal.js exists
  measure  total  number after "Total Iterations:"
  measure  keep  number after "Keep wins:"
  measure  change  number after "Change wins:"
  rule     total is 10000000
  rule     keep is between 3200000 and 3500000
  rule     change is between 6500000 and 6800000
  note     the bands are the v0 run's 0.32-0.35 and 0.65-0.68 multiplied by the
  note     iteration count, which `total` pins. The direct reading -- the second
  note     "Win percent:" in the output -- is not expressible: an extractor
  note     anchored to a label takes the first match, and there is no way to say
  note     "the second one", nor to say "change is above keep"
  because  Monty Hall is 1/3 keep and 2/3 switch, an outside truth that does not
  because  depend on any of this code being right

heuristic texas-selfcheck
  run      node texas.js
  seed     20260905
  timeout  600000
  applies  when texas.js exists
  measure  status  exit code
  measure  failures  count of lines matching "FAIL"
  rule     status is 0
  rule     failures is 0
  because  the project's own self-check, adopted as-is: no new assertions to
  because  write, and it rides along every replay for free
